===Articles and determiner===
There is no equivalent for the definite article ''the'', and the indefinite article ''a'' is further inflected as masculine or feminine with its object.<!-- a guess to what was meant-->

==Pronouns==
The [[Grammatical person|second person]] nominative pronoun 'you' is expressed two different ways: the polite form {{Transliteration|mby|aaen}} (cognate with {{Transliteration|sd|avheen}} in standard Sindhi), generally used for respected strangers, the elderly, parents and older relatives, and the familiar form {{Transliteration|mby|tu}}, used among close friends and when addressing subordinates. The [[Object (grammar)|accusative]], [[possessive pronouns|possessive]] and [[reflexive pronoun|reflexive]] pronouns are often [[Inflection|inflected]] for [[Grammatical gender|masculine and feminine]] and their gender must agree with their referents.

See also: [[b:Urdu:Pronouns|Urdu pronouns]]

